abstract: >-
  Donghyunwar is a browser-based, noncommercial medieval turn-based tactics
  laboratory for one player against a computer opponent (Imperial Age with
  all technologies researched, no fog of war). The map, civilizations, first
  move, starting resources and seed are chosen only through programs written
  in the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang; the battle itself is
  played with the keyboard or on-screen buttons. It includes five
  civilizations, 27 unit types plus five heroes, six original maps, building
  income and production, monks that heal and convert, market mercenaries, an
  approximate damage formula, a heuristic computer opponent, and saving and
  loading. Its rule framework and unit names and numbers follow the Nintendo
  DS game Age of Empires: The Age of Kings (2006); it contains none of that
  game's graphics, sound, maps or text. Age of Empires is a trademark of
  Microsoft Corporation; this work is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  Microsoft, Majesco or Backbone Entertainment. The MIT license applies to the
  application code, documentation and artwork only; the fonts are under the
  SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
